> 
> Here's the questions
> 
> 1. I want to mirror the two 18 GB drives for root, usr etc. Should I
> use LSM ?
> 
Personally I never saw a good reason for using LSM when I had hardware
RAID. Why not put the drives on the KZPCC and use hardware mirroring? LSM
works, but hardware raid works too.

> 2. I want the dsk numbering to start with the internal drives, any
> issue with
> powering down the drives attached to the kzpcc and configuring them
> later ?
> They want to be dsk0 and 1 if i dont.
> 
You can change the disk numbers with dsfmgr after the build is complete,
but no there is no problem with doing it your way if you are using the
internal disks. Personally I would have it all behind the RAID controller
and be done with it.


> 3. any suggestions on kernel configuation ? I dont need ATM, all
> commuications
> out of the box will be tcp/ip on the 1Gbs card.
> 
Oracle have some recommendations for the kernel paramters that are fairly
important, look them up.
Otherwise just install it all, with 32Gb of RAM it will make such a tiny
difference that it isn't worth the effort of deciding what to chop.

Adam


